{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (78.95%) to predicted seq8 V=L=F=R: 11%, K: 28%. Activity: Active against A. baumannii ATCC 19606 (MIC 8 ug/ml), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 8 ug/ml), K. pneumoniae ATCC 700603 (MIC 16 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa CMCC 10104 (MIC 32 ug/ml), S. aureus ATCC 25923 or MRSA (MIC 4 ug/ml). Inhibited bacterial attachment, inhibited biofilm formation (64 uM), disrupted biofilms. Structure: random coil in water and helical in 30 mM SDS but not helical in 50% TFE (SDS-TFE).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "41184786", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "BMC microbiology, 25(1), 707. https://doi.org/10.1186/s12866-025-04343-3. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05932", "source_id": "AP05932", "source_numeric_id": "05932", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05932", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Novel antibacterial peptide HfAMP against methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
